  <h2 id="which-to-choose">Which FPS Should You Download?</h2>
  <p>If you are downloading a movie or cinematic short, stick to the original frame rate (usually 24fps or 30fps). Downloading a movie that has been artificially upscaled to 60fps will ruin the cinematic feel and waste storage space.</p>
  <p>If you are downloading a video game walkthrough or a sports highlight, downloading the 60fps version (if available) will provide a significantly better viewing experience.</p>
